      "q": "2. Calculate the molarity of a solution prepared by mixing 500 mL of 2.5 M urea solution and 500 mL of 2M urea solution.",
      "a": "Given that,\n$${{M}_{1}}=2.5M$$\n$${{M}_{2}}=2M$$\n$${{V}_{1}}={{V}_{2}}=500ml$$\nNow, by the law of dilution, we get;\n$$M=\\frac{{{M}_{1}}{{V}_{1}}+{{M}_{2}}{{V}_{2}}}{{{V}_{1}}+{{V}_{2}}}$$\n$$M=\\frac{\\left( 2.5+2 \\right)\\times 500}{1000}$$\nThus, molarity of the solution = 2.25 M."
