      "q": "6. The solubility of oxygen in water is $1.35\\times {{10}^{-3}}mol{{L}^{-1}}$at $20{}^\\circ C$\u00a0 and 1 atm pressure. Calculate the concentration of oxygen at $20{}^\\circ C$ and 0.2 atm pressure.",
      "a": "Given that,\n$$C=1.35\\times {{10}^{-3}}mol{{L}^{-1}}$$\nP = 1 atm\nWe know the Henry\u2019s law;\n$$C={{K}_{H}}P$$\nThus,\n$${{K}_{H}}=\\frac{C}{P}=1.35\\times {{10}^{-3}}Mat{{m}^{-1}}$$\nNow, at 0.2 atm;\n$$C=1.35\\times {{10}^{-3}}\\times 0.2$$\n$$C=2.7\\times {{10}^{-3}}M$$"
