      "q": "14. Osmotic pressure of a 0.0103 molar solution of an electrolyte was found to be 0.75 atm at $27{}^\\circ C$ . Calculate Van\u2019t Hoff factor.",
      "a": "Given that,\n$$\\pi =0.75atm$$\n$$C=0.0103m$$\n$$R=0.0820Latmmo{{l}^{-1}}{{K}^{-1}}$$\n$$T=27{}^\\circ C=300K$$\nBy the formula of osmotic pressure, we get;\n$$\\pi =iCRT$$\n$$\\therefore i=\\frac{\\pi }{CRT}=\\frac{0.75}{0.0103\\times 0.082\\times 300}=2.95$$"
