      "q": "30.\nThe rate of a reaction quadruples when the temperature changes from 293 K to 313\nK. Calculate the energy of activation of the reaction if it does not change with temperature.",
      "a": "From Arrhenius equation, we get\n$\\log , \\log \\dfrac{k_{2}}{k_{1}}=\\dfrac{E_{a}}{2.303}\\left(\\dfrac{T_{2}-T_{1}}{T_{1} T_{2}}\\right)$\nGiven\n$k_{2}=4 k_{1}$\n$T_{1}=293 \\mathrm{~K} $\n$ T_{2}=313 \\mathrm{~K} $\n${\\text{ So }, \\log \\dfrac{4 k_{2}}{k_{1}}=\\dfrac{E_{a}}{2.303 \\times 8.314}\\left(\\dfrac{313-293}{293 \\times 313}\\right)}$\n$0.6021=\\dfrac{20 \\times E_{a}}{2.303 \\times 8.314 \\times 293 \\times 313} $\n$E_{a}=\\dfrac{0.6021 \\times 2.303 \\times 8.314 \\times 293 \\times 313}{20} $\n$=52863.00 \\mathrm{~J} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$\n$=52.86 \\mathrm{k} \\mathrm{J} \\mathrm{mol}^{-1}$\nAs a result, the activation energy required is $52.86 \\mathrm{k} \\mathrm{J} \\mathrm{mol}^{-1}$\nWe hope, these important questions have helped you in brushing up on your concepts related to\nClass 12 Chemistry Chapter 3\n. You must practice solving these questions regularly to be more clear with the chapter as well as the chemical formulas. Utilise your coming days smartly by following the important study materials provided above and sit for your\nCBSE Board exams\nconfidently.\nRelated Study Materials for Class 12 Chemistry Chapter 3\nS.No\nImportant Study Material Links for Class 12 Chemistry Chapter 3"
