      "q": "18. Account for the following:\n(a) Transition metals and the majority of their compounds act as good catalysts.\nAns.\nTransition metals and their compounds are effective catalysts because of their ability to exhibit changing oxidation states and form complexes, as well as the fact that they give a suitable surface for reaction to occur. For example, in the contact process, vanadium oxide is used, while in Haber's Process, finely split iron is used.\n(b) From element to element, actinoid contraction is greater than lanthanoid contraction.\nAns.\nDue to inadequate shielding by ${\\text{5f}}$-electrons in actinoids compared to ${\\text{4f}}$-electrons in lanthanoids, actinoid contraction is higher than lanthanoid contraction from element to element.",
