      "q": "5. Calculate the magnetic moments of the following complexes:\n(i)[Fe(CN)\n6\n]\n4-\nAns.\nThe oxidation state of central iron is +2. So, the Fe\n2+\nis a\u00a0 3d\n6\ncomplex. As,\nCN\n\u2212\nis a strong field ligand, the electron gets paired up and hence no unpaired\u00a0 electron is present. The magnetic moment will be:\n$\\begin{aligned}&\\mu_{B H}=\\sqrt{\\mathrm{n}(\\mathrm{n}+2)} \\\\&\\mu_{B H}=0\\end{aligned}$\n(ii) [CoF\n6\n]\n3-\nAns.\nThe oxidation state of central cobalt is +3. So, the\nCo\n+3\nis a 3d\n5\ncomplex.\nAs fluoride is a weak field ligand, there will be no pairing in the electrons. So, n = 5\n$\\begin{aligned}&\\mu_{B H}=\\sqrt{\\mathrm{n}(\\mathrm{n}+2)} \\\\&\\mu_{B H}=\\sqrt{5(5+2)} \\\\ &\\mu_{B H}=5.9 \\mathrm{~B} \\cdot\\mathrm{M}\\end{aligned}$",
