      "q": "6. How will you bring about the following conversions?\nBenzene to Aniline\nAns.\nThe conversion of benzene to aniline is as followed:\nAniline to benzene\nAns.\nThe conversion of aniline to benzene is as followed:\nEthanoic acid to ethanamine\nAns.\nThe conversion of ethanoic acid to ethanamine is as followed:\n${\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{COOH}}\\xrightarrow{{{\\text{N}}{{\\text{H}}_3}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{CO}}{{\\text{O}}^ - }{\\text{N}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{4}}}^ + \\xrightarrow[\\Delta ]{}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{CON}}{{\\text{H}}_2}\\xrightarrow{{{\\text{LiAl}}{{\\text{H}}_4}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{N}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}\\,$\np-toluidine to 2-bromo-4-methylaniline\nAns\n. The conversion of p-toluidine to 2-bromo-4-methylaniline is as followed:\nMethylbromide to ethanamine\nAns.\nThe conversion of methylbromide to ethanamine is as followed:\n${\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{Br\u00a0 +\u00a0 KCN}} \\to {\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{CN\u00a0 +\u00a0 KBr}}$\n${\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{CN\u00a0 +\u00a0 4[H]}}\\xrightarrow[{{\\text{Alc}}{\\text{.}}}]{{{\\text{Na}}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{N}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}$\nBenzenediazonium chloride to nitrobenzene\nAns.\nThe conversion of benzenediazonium chloride to nitrobenzene is as followed:\nEthylamine to methylamine\nAns.\nThe conversion of ethylamine to methylamine is as followed:\n$${\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{N}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}\\xrightarrow{{{\\text{HN}}{{\\text{O}}_2}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{OH}}\\xrightarrow{{{\\text{[O]}}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{COOH}}\\xrightarrow{{{\\text{PC}}{{\\text{l}}_5}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{COCl}}\\xrightarrow{{{\\text{N}}{{\\text{H}}_3}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{CON}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}\\xrightarrow{{{\\text{B}}{{\\text{r}}_2}/{\\text{KOH}}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{N}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}$$\nBenzene to sulphanilic acid\nAns.\nThe conversion of benzene to sulphanilic acid is as followed:\nHexanenitrile to 1-aminopentane\nAns.\nThe conversion of hexanenitrile to 1-aminopentane is as followed:\n${{\\text{C}}_{\\text{5}}}{{\\text{H}}_{{\\text{11}}}}{\\text{CN}}\\xrightarrow{{{{\\text{H}}^ + }/{{\\text{H}}_2}{\\text{O}}}}{{\\text{C}}_{\\text{5}}}{{\\text{H}}_{{\\text{11}}}}{\\text{COOH}}\\xrightarrow{{{\\text{SOC}}{{\\text{l}}_2}}}{{\\text{C}}_{\\text{5}}}{{\\text{H}}_{{\\text{11}}}}{\\text{COCl}}\\xrightarrow[{{\\text{Excess}}}]{{{\\text{N}}{{\\text{H}}_3}}}{{\\text{C}}_{\\text{5}}}{{\\text{H}}_{{\\text{11}}}}{\\text{CON}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}\\xrightarrow{{{\\text{B}}{{\\text{r}}_2}/{\\text{KOH}}}}{{\\text{C}}_{\\text{5}}}{{\\text{H}}_{{\\text{11}}}}{\\text{N}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}$",
